Participants were students and members of staff at a University of Applied Sciences in southern Germany (N=72), 54 males (Mage = 24.91, SDage = 4.27) and 18 female (Mage = 26.39, SDage = 7.26). They were randomly assigned to either the treatment (n=36: FVA) or the control group (n=36: LVA). The SE of the control group included basic visual elements such as buildings, traffic signs, and traffic lights. The treatment group's SE additionally included walking pedestrians and many randomly driving cars. Figure 2 shows gender distribution of the participants.
